    "title": "Measurements of the Semileptonic Decays $\\bar{B}\\to D\\ell\\bar{\\nu}$ and $\\bar{B}\\to D^{*}\\ell\\bar{\\nu}$ Using a Global Fit to $DX\\ell\\bar{\\nu}$ Final States",
    "arxiv": "[hep-ex/0809.0828v2](https://arxiv.org/pdf/0809.0828)",
    "time": "2008.09.04",
    "abstract": "Semileptonic $\\bar{B}$ decays to $DX\\ell\\bar{\\nu}$ ($\\ell=e$ or $\\mu$) are selected by reconstructing $D^{0}\\ell$ and $D^{+}\\ell$ combinations from a sample of 230 million $\\Upsilon(4S) \\to B\\bar{B}$ decays recorded with the BaBar detector at the PEP-II $e^{+}e^{-}$ collider at SLAC. A global fit to these samples is used to extract the branching fractions $\\mathcal{B}(B^{-}\\to D^{0}\\ell\\bar{\\nu})$ and $\\mathcal{B}(B^{-}\\to D^{*0}\\ell\\bar{\\nu})$, the form-factor slope parameters $\\rho_{D}^{2}$ and $\\rho_{D^{*}}^{2}$, and the products $\\mathcal{G}(1)|V_{cb}|$ and $\\mathcal{F}(1)|V_{cb}|$.",
